  "vowel_alternation": "The two ai-final teaching forms are ā-final before this non-śit ending by 6.1.45. Both start in a conjunct and neither is in the compulsory group of 6.4.67. Since active āśīrliṅ acts as kit under 3.4.104, 6.4.68 admits ā and e at all nine slots of each root. Compare glāyāt/gleyāt, compulsory stheyāt and simple yāyāt in the Kāśikā. These ā/e choices occur without san or caṅ and without a ti copy.",
  "dh_alternation": "The four selected middle stems receive iṭ before sīyuṭ. The preceding sounds are h of māh, and y in the other three stems after the ṇic vowel has the ay form. On the received iṇ-based reading these allow the two 2pl outputs dh/ḍh under 8.3.79. The two separate i vowels belong to iṭ and the blessing suffix complex.",
  "other_P": "P before yāsuṭ has no outer iṭ. On the two P curādi inputs the causative i disappears before the unaugmented ending under 6.4.51. Short radical a of mah and inherited ā of nāṭ remain independent root decisions. The 2sg has no added personal s after the inherited ending schedule.",
